  "slug": "cooperation-decoding-microbial-4ea5",
  "summary": "Long-read and single-cell sequencing expand variant calling into new platforms, creating need for reference standards and validation tooling.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is accuracy assessment of variant-level calls. LoReC compares and annotates structural variants across short-read, long-read and optical mapping data against the T2T reference, and a cancer genome benchmark evaluates Oxford Nanopore somatic calling against short-read data using cell line mixtures across tumour purities and depths. NEXT-scASV performs de novo allele-specific calling from 5' scRNA-seq, validated on 135,000 PBMCs from 57 donors. TrioDNM and VRFS reduce false positives in de novo mutation calling relative to DeNovoGear, and CNValidatron automates validation of PennCNV array calls using a CNN trained on human-verified visual calls, with ~90% performance. What is new is the emphasis on benchmark standards and validation tooling spanning platforms, with the cell line mixtures serving as concrete reference standards.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
